Left over from k342 (secrets worker, 2026-10-31). k342 made `OCP::ErrorLine::one_line` the one helper that turns an exception into a single STDERR line. Two callers use it so far: Init's `_catalogue_error` and the Machines role's `_oneline`. Other places still strip Perl source locations by hand. The line numbers below are on the k342 base:

- lib/OCP/Cmd/Apply/Drift.pm:1229
- lib/OCP/Cmd/Status.pm:531
- lib/OCP/Cmd/Init.pm:741 and :800
- lib/OCP.pm:235 (run_cli: check first whether its job differs, since it tells user errors from internal ones by the location)

Done = each one either calls `one_line` (with `mask =>` where a secret is in play), or has a comment saying why it can't. Only the visible edge case changes: a wrapped error's inner " at FILE line N." no longer stays in the line. Tests: the callers' existing tests stay green; add one case per converted site where a location in the middle used to survive.

Lane: cross-cutting → ocp-worker. Low priority. Depends on k342 being committed.

